#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/glossary.md:10
msgid ""
"Ever wondered what we mean by a specific term? We've been collecting the "
"most relevant terms below for your insight."
msgstr ""
"Да ли сте се икада запитали шта подразумевамо под одређеним термином? "
"Прикупили смо најрелевантније термине у наставку за ваш увид."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/glossary.md:12
#, no-wrap
msgid "<VPGlossary>\n"
msgstr "<VPGlossary>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/glossary.md:19
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Admin\n"
": An admin(istrator) is a user in Zammad who has special rights and manages your\n"
"  Zammad. An admin can, for example, configure user permissions, time recording\n"
"  settings, automation and text modules.\n"
"  If you're looking for someone to adjust anything in your Zammad, your admin\n"
"  is the right person to ask for.\n"
msgstr ""
"Admin\n"
": Administrator je korisnik u Zammadu koji ima posebna prava i upravlja vašim\n"
"  Zammadom. Administrator može na primer da konfiguriše dozvole korisnika, podešavanja\n"
"  evidentiranja vremena, automatizaciju i module za tekst.\n"
"  Ako tražite osobu koja će prilagoditi bilo šta u vašem Zammadu, vaš administrator\n"
"  je osoba koju treba da kontaktirate.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/glossary.md:24
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Agent\n"
": An agent is a user in Zammad who works on tickets and responds to customer\n"
"  inquiries. Agents can be admins too, meaning that they can change settings,\n"
"  user permissions and so on (see above).\n"
msgstr ""
"Agent\n"
": Agent je korisnik u Zammadu koji radi na slučajevima i odgovara na upite\n"
"  kupaca. Agenti mogu biti i administratori, što znači da mogu da menjaju podešavanja,\n"
"  dozvole korisnika i slično (vidi gore).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/glossary.md:30
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"API\n"
": An API (Application Programming Interface) is a set of rules and protocols\n"
"  that allow different software applications to communicate with each other.\n"
"  It allows you to connect third party systems with your Zammad (e.g. social\n"
"  media, messengers, monitoring tools).\n"
msgstr ""
"API\n"
": API (Programerski interfejs aplikacije) je skup pravila i protokola\n"
"  koji omogućavaju različitim softverskim aplikacijama da komuniciraju jedna sa drugom.\n"
"  Omogućava vam da povezete sisteme trećih strana sa svojim Zammadom (npr. društvene\n"
"  mreže, mesindžere, alate za monitoring).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/glossary.md:34
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  You can learn more on our\n"
"  [API landing page](https://zammad.com/en/product/features/rest-api){target=_blank}\n"
"  as well as in our [API reference](/en/reference/rest-api/intro).\n"
msgstr ""
"  Više možete saznati na našoj\n"
"  [landing stranici API-ja](https://zammad.com/en/product/features/rest-api){target=_blank}\n"
"  kao i u našem [referentnom priručniku za API](/en/reference/rest-api/intro).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/glossary.md:40
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Article\n"
": Each item within a ticket is called article. Ticket articles\n"
"  can be internal (only agents can see them) or public\n"
"  (customers can see them too; e.g. public notes or outgoing emails) and include\n"
"  formatted text as well as attachments and inline images.\n"
msgstr ""
"Članak\n"
": Svaka stavka unutar slučaja naziva se članak. Članci u slučajevima\n"
"  mogu biti interni (vidljivi samo agenticima) ili javni\n"
"  (vidljivi i kupcima; npr. javne napomene ili odlazna elektronska pošta) i uključuju\n"
"  formatirani tekst kao i priloge i ugněždene slike.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/glossary.md:48
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Automation\n"
": There are many processes that can be automated with Zammad.\n"
"  This means that certain actions take place automatically.\n"
"  An automation can be time-based or action-based and should cover every\n"
"  conceivable automation scenario.\n"
"  An example could be the recurring deletion of customers who are no longer\n"
"  needed or the assignment of groups based on ticket attributes.\n"
msgstr ""
"Automatizacija\n"
": Postoji mnogo procesa koji se mogu automatizovati pomoću Zammada.\n"
"  To znači da se određene radnje izvršavaju automatski.\n"
"  Automatizacija može biti vremenski ili akciono bazirana i treba da pokrije svaki\n"
"  zamislivi scenario automatizacije.\n"
"  Primer može biti periodično brisanje korisnika koji više nisu potrebni\n"
"  ili dodeljivanje grupa na osnovu atributa slučaja.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/glossary.md:54
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Autosave\n"
": Zammad's autosave feature makes sure that no work is lost. So if your browser\n"
"  crashes, simply log in again and resume where you were before.\n"
"  Learn more on our\n"
"  [Autosave landing page](https://zammad.com/en/product/features/autosave){target=_blank}.\n"
msgstr ""
"Automatsko čuvanje\n"
": Funkcija automatskog čuvanja u Zammadu osigurava da se rad ne izgubi. Dakle, ako vaš pretraživač\n"
"  padne, jednostavno se ponovo ulogujte i nastavite tačno odakle ste stali.\n"
"  Saznajte više na našoj\n"
"  [landing stranici za automatsko čuvanje](https://zammad.com/en/product/features/autosave){target=_blank}.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/glossary.md:58
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Branding\n"
": Every company has a different identity. This is why Zammad lets you add your\n"
"  logo, signature, links and other things!\n"
msgstr ""
"Brendiranje\n"
": Svaka kompanija ima drugačiji identitet. Zbog toga vam Zammad omogućava da dodate svoj\n"
"  logo, potpis, linkove i druge elemente!\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/glossary.md:62
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Changelog\n"
": With every new release comes a new changelog. It is basically a list of all\n"
"  the things that have changed, from new enhancements to bug fixes.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dnevnik promena\n"
": Svako novo izdanje donosi novi dnevnik promena. To je zapravo spisak svega\n"
"  što se promenilo, od novih poboljšanja do ispravki grešaka.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/glossary.md:65
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  You can find them all on our\n"
"  [GitHub](https://github.com/zammad/zammad/blob/stable/CHANGELOG.md){target=_blank}!\n"
msgstr ""
"  Све их можете пронаћи на нашој\n"
"  [GitHub страни](https://github.com/zammad/zammad/blob/stable/CHANGELOG.md){target=_blank}!\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/glossary.md:71
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Checkmk\n"
": Checkmk is a powerful IT monitoring tool that can send real-time status\n"
"  alerts to Zammad via email or REST API. Set these alerts up in Checkmk,\n"
"  and Zammad will automatically create, update and close tickets based on\n"
"  the health of your system.\n"
msgstr ""
"Checkmk\n"
": Checkmk je moćan alat za IT monitoring koji može da šalje upozorenja o statusu\n"
"  u realnom vremenu do Zammada putem elektronske pošte ili REST API-ja. Podesite ova upozorenja u Checkmku,\n"
"  a Zammad će automatski stvarati, ažurirati i zatvarati slučajeve na osnovu\n"
"  zdravlja vašeg sistema.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/glossary.md:77
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Clearbit\n"
": Clearbit is a service designed to collect information on your\n"
"  contacts. Thus, new queries from unknown users in Zammad can be automatically\n"
"  enriched with information such as company, number of employees,\n"
"  annual turnover, industry and much more.\n"
msgstr ""
"Clearbit\n"
": Clearbit je servis dizajniran za prikupljanje informacija o vašim\n"
"  kontaktima. Tako se novi upiti nepoznatih korisnika u Zammadu mogu automatski\n"
"  obogatiti informacijama poput kompanije, broja zaposlenih,\n"
"  godišnjeg prometa, industrije i mnogo toga drugog.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/glossary.md:84
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Conflict Warning\n"
": When two agents edit the same ticket at the same time, a lot can go wrong -\n"
"  from duplicate replies to overwritten messages. Zammad helps you to avoid\n"
"  this with its integrated conflict warning. So if you see another agent's\n"
"  avatar and a little pen at the bottom of your ticket, it means the other agent\n"
"  is currently editing it.\n"
msgstr ""
"Upozorenje na sukob\n"
": Kada dva agenta istovremeno uređuju isti slučaj, mnogo toga može poći po zlu -\n"
"  od duplikata odgovora do prepisanih poruka. Zammad vam pomaže da izbegnete\n"
"  ovo zahvaljujući integrisanom upozorenju na sukob. Dakle, ako vidite avatar drugog agenta\n"
"  i malu olovku na dnu slučaja, to znači da ga drugi agent trenutno uređuje.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/glossary.md:88
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Content Sidebar\n"
": Right sidebar in the ticket view which includes the sidebar tabs and the\n"
"  active sidebar (if opened).\n"
msgstr ""
"Sadržaj trake\n"
": Desna traka u prikazu tiketa koja uključuje kartice trake i\n"
"  aktivnu traku (ako je otvorena).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/glossary.md:94
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Core Workflows\n"
": This feature allows you to configure dynamic fields and ticket masks based on\n"
"  attribute available in Zammad. For example you can disable or hide fields,\n"
"  make them visible based on other fields or attributes, make them mandatory and\n"
"  much more!\n"
msgstr ""
"Osnovni radni tokovi\n"
": Ova funkcija omogućava vam konfigurisanje dinamičkih polja i maski tiketa na osnovu\n"
"  atributa dostupnih u Zammad-u. Na primer, možete onemogućiti ili sakriti polja,\n"
"  učiniti ih vidljivim na osnovu drugih polja ili atributa, učiniti ih obaveznim i\n"
"  mnogo više!\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/glossary.md:100
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"CTI\n"
": CTI stands for Computer Telephony Integration and allows you to collect\n"
"  detailed information on all your incoming and outgoing calls.\n"
"  This includes, for example, a call log, an overview of which agent is\n"
"  currently on a call, a caller ID search, and even a Do-Not-Disturb-Mode.\n"
msgstr ""
"CTI\n"
": CTI označava Computer Telephony Integration i omogućava prikupljanje\n"
"  detaljnih informacija o svim vašim ulaznim i izlaznim pozivima.\n"
"  To uključuje, na primer, evidenciju poziva, pregled kojeg agenta je\n"
"  trenutno na pozivu, pretragu broja pozivaoca, pa čak i Do-Not-Disturb-Mode.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/glossary.md:109
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Custom Development (CD)\n"
": We are constantly working on improving Zammad, and we keep adding new\n"
"  features with every single release. However, sometimes our customers might\n"
"  require a very specific new feature, addition, or adjustment that is either\n"
"  very urgent or very particular to their individual use case.\n"
"  This is when a custom development can take place: We offer the customer to\n"
"  develop the desired feature at a price that we agree upon previously\n"
"  (which is based on the expected hours needed for completion).\n"
msgstr ""
"Prilagođeni razvoj (CD)\n"
": Kontinuirano radimo na unapređenju Zammada i dodajemo nove\n"
"  funkcije sa svakim izdanjem. Međutim, ponekad naši kupci mogu\n"
"  zahtevati veoma specifičnu novu funkciju, dodatak ili prilagodbu koja je ili\n"
"  veoma hitna ili veoma specifična za njihov pojedinačni slučaj upotrebe.\n"
"  Tada može doći do prilagođenog razvoja: nudimo kupcu da\n"
"  razvije željenu funkciju po ceni na koju se unapred dogovorimo\n"
"  (koja je zasnovana na očekivanom broju sati potrebnih za završetak).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/glossary.md:117
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Customer\n"
": A customer is a person you communicate with via Zammad.\n"
"  For each customer there is a profile page showing all the tickets and more\n"
"  information. Customers can be assigned to one or more organizations.\n"
"  Each customer can access their individual\n"
"  Customer Interface, where they see all their tickets with the current\n"
"  status and live updates.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kupac\n"
": Kupac je osoba s kojom komunicirate putem Zammada.\n"
"  Za svakog kupca postoji strana profila koja prikazuje sve tikete i više\n"
"  informacija. Kupci se mogu dodeliti jednoj ili više organizacija.\n"
"  Svaki kupac može pristupiti svom individualnom\n"
"  Korisničkom interfejsu, gde vidi sve svoje tikete sa trenutnim\n"
"  statusom i ažuriranjima u realnom vremenu.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/glossary.md:124
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Dashboard\n"
": The dashboard is the individual welcome page in Zammad and gives\n"
"  you feedback about your work.\n"
"  Here you can find all sorts of overviews, such as the open tickets,\n"
"  the average waiting time, or the reopening rate. You can also see what your\n"
"  colleagues are doing by checking the Activity Stream.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kontrolna tabla\n"
": Kontrolna tabla je individualna početna strana u Zammad-u i daje\n"
"  povratne informacije o vašem radu.\n"
"  Ovde možete pronaći razne preglede, kao što su otvoreni tiketi,\n"
"  prosek vremena čekanja ili stopa ponovnog otvaranja. Takođe možete videti šta vaši\n"
"  kolege rade proverom aktivnosti tokova.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/glossary.md:129
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Dialog\n"
": A dialog is a element which pops up in the middle of the screen because of its\n"
"  importance. An example could be the dialog which asks you to save or discard\n"
"  your unsaved changes.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dijalog\n"
": Dijalog je element koji se pojavljuje u sredini ekrana zbog svoje\n"
"  važnosti. Primer može biti dijalog koji vas pita da li želite da sačuvate ili odbacite\n"
"  nesaučuvane izmene.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/glossary.md:133
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Documentation\n"
": You probably have noticed already: you are reading a part of Zammad's\n"
"  documentation. 😉\n"
msgstr ""
"Dokumentacija\n"
": Verovatno ste već primetili: čitate deo dokumentacije Zammada. 😉\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/glossary.md:139
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Elasticsearch\n"
": Zammad offers an Elasticsearch integration (a free and open search engine)\n"
"  that makes the search process within Zammad super fast and powerful. You\n"
"  can even connect a reporting tool like Grafana to your Elasticsearch to\n"
"  create powerful reports and statistics.\n"
msgstr ""
"Elasticsearch\n"
": Zammad nudi integraciju sa Elasticsearch-om (besplatnim i otvorenim sistemom za pretragu)\n"
"  koji čini proces pretrage unutar Zammada izuzetno brzim i moćnim. Možete\n"
"  čak povezati alat za izveštavanje kao što je Grafana sa vašim Elasticsearch-om da\n"
"  kreirate napredne izveštaje i statistike.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/glossary.md:144
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Escalation\n"
": An escalation is what happens after the deadline for a ticket has passed. You\n"
"  can configure it within Zammad's SLA (Service Level Agreement) feature. An\n"
"  escalated ticket is marked red in your taskbar and the overviews.\n"
msgstr ""
"Eskalacija\n"
": Eskalacija je ono što se dešava nakon što istekne rok za tike. Možete\n"
"  ga podesiti unutar Zammadove SLA (Service Level Agreement) funkcije. Tike\n"
"  koji je eskaliran označen je crveno u vašoj traci zadataka i pregledima.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/glossary.md:150
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Exchange Integration\n"
": The Exchange integration allows you to sync your contacts from your\n"
"  Exchange address book to Zammad. Every time a contact is updated\n"
"  in Exchange, it will be reflected in Zammad. This gives you direct\n"
"  access to all your contacts in your Zammad.\n"
msgstr ""
"Integracija sa Exchangem\n"
": Integracija sa Exchangem omogućava sinhronizaciju vaših kontakata iz imenika\n"
"  Exchanga u Zammad. Svaki put kada se kontakt ažurira\n"
"  u Exchange-u, to će se odraziti u Zammad-u. Ovo vam daje direktan\n"
"  pristup svim vašim kontaktima unutar Zammada.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/glossary.md:157
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"External Authentication\n"
": External authentication is an easy, one-click option for your users to log\n"
"  into Zammad. It has various benefits: not only is it faster but it also\n"
"  means that your users will have to remember fewer passwords.\n"
"  Zammad currently supports more than ten login providers, such as Facebook,\n"
"  GitHub, GitLab, Google, or Microsoft.\n"
msgstr ""
"Spoljašna autentifikacija\n"
": Spoljašna autentifikacija je jednostavna opcija jednim klikom za vaše korisnike da se\n"
"  prijave u Zammad. Ima brojne prednosti: nije samo brža, već znači\n"
"  da će vaši korisnici morati da pamte manje lozinki.\n"
"  Zammad trenutno podržava više od deset provajdera prijavljivanja, kao što su Facebook,\n"
"  GitHub, GitLab, Google ili Microsoft.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/glossary.md:162
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Feature\n"
": A feature is a specific capability or functionality that Zammad provides to\n"
"  you such as our integrations, productivity tools or additional channels.\n"
"  We keep adding new features with every release.\n"
msgstr ""
"Funkcionalnost\n"
": Funkcionalnost je specifična mogućnost ili funkcija koju Zammad pruža\n"
"  vama, kao što su naše integracije, alati za produktivnost ili dodatni kanali.\n"
"  Svako izdanje donosi nove funkcionalnosti.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/glossary.md:169
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Feature Request\n"
": You can let us know if you are missing a particular feature in Zammad.\n"
"  We collect all of your wishes in our community forum in the\n"
"  [feature request category](https://community.zammad.org/c/stuff-you-like-zammad-to-have-feel-free-to-discuss-and-add-proposals/6/all){target=_blank}.\n"
"  If a request comes in regularly and we think that it would be a\n"
"  great addition, we'll put it on our roadmap and start working on it.\n"
msgstr ""
"Zahtev za funkcionalnost\n"
": Možete nam javiti ako vam nedostaje određena funkcionalnost u Zammad-u.\n"
"  Sva vaša želja sakupljamo na našem zajedničkom forumu u\n"
"  [kategoriji za zahteve](https://community.zammad.org/c/stuff-you-like-zammad-to-have-feel-free-to-discuss-and-add-proposals/6/all){target=_blank}.\n"
"  Ako se zahtev redovno javlja i smatramo da bi bio\n"
"  odličan dodatak, staviti ćemo ga na naš put razvoja i početi da radimo na njemu.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/glossary.md:174
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Feature Sponsoring\n"
": If an organization urgently requires one of the features on the list,\n"
"  they can fast-forward the development and put it on top of the list by\n"
"  sponsoring it, which means that they cover the costs for the development.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sponzorisanje funkcionalnosti\n"
": Ako organizacija hitno zahteva jednu od funkcionalnosti sa liste,\n"
"  može ubrzati razvoj i staviti je na vrh liste sponzorišući je, što znači da pokrivaju troškove razvoja.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/glossary.md:179
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"GitHub\n"
": GitHub is a service for the version management of software development\n"
"  projects. It uses Git, a software that tracks changes in file sets.\n"
"  Here at Zammad, we use it to maintain and enhance our code.\n"
msgstr ""
"GitHub\n"
": GitHub je usluga za upravljanje verzijama softverskih razvojnih\n"
"  projekata. Koristi Git, program koji prati izmene u skupovima fajlova.\n"
"  U Zammad-u ga koristimo za održavanje i unapređenje našeg koda.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/glossary.md:183
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  As Zammad is an open-source project, many developers and tech-lovers from all\n"
"  over the world contribute to it. GitHub is where we coordinate all of this.\n"
"  Follow the link to find [our repositories](https://github.com/zammad){target=_blank}.\n"
msgstr ""
"  Pošto je Zammad projekat otvorenog koda, mnogi programeri i ljubitelji tehnologije sa svih\n"
"  delova sveta mu doprinose. GitHub je mesto gde koordiniramo sve ovo.\n"
"  Pritisnite na link da pronađete [naše repozitorijume](https://github.com/zammad){target=_blank}.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/glossary.md:187
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  Besides our own repos, Zammad also has an integration for GitHub.\n"
"  Using it allows you to show all relevant information about your\n"
"  issues directly in a sidebar tab, such as status or assignees.\n"
msgstr ""
"  Pored sopstvenih repozitorijuma, Zammad takođe ima integraciju za GitHub.\n"
"  Njeno korišćenje vam omogućava da prikažete sve relevantne informacije o vašim\n"
"  problemima direktno u kartici bočne trake, kao što su status ili dodeljeni.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/glossary.md:191
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"GitLab\n"
": GitLab is similar to GitHub.\n"
"  Here at Zammad, we use it for our internal development.\n"
msgstr ""
"GitLab\n"
": GitLab je sličan GitHub-u.\n"
"  U Zammad-u ga koristimo za naš interni razvoj.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/glossary.md:195
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  There is also an integration that allows users to connect GitLab to Zammad\n"
"  so that all their issues and their corresponding changes are reflected in\n"
"  Zammad's sidebar tab as well.\n"
msgstr ""
"  Postoji i integracija koja omogućava korisnicima da povežu GitLab sa Zammad-om\n"
"  tako da se svi njihovi problemi i odgovarajuće izmene odražavaju u\n"
"  kartici bočne trake Zammada.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/glossary.md:200
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Grafana\n"
": Grafana is an open-source reporting tool. It Elasticsearch as data source.\n"
"  Hosted customers with a Plus plan can use it to get detailed statistics of\n"
"  their instance. Self hosting Zammad users can use Grafana as well.\n"
msgstr ""
"Grafana\n"
": Grafana je alat za izveštavanje otvorenog koda. Koristi Elasticsearch kao izvor podataka.\n"
"  Hostovani korisnici sa Plus planom mogu ga koristiti za detaljne statistike svoje\n"
"  instance. Korisnici Zammada koji hostuju sami takođe mogu koristiti Grafana.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/glossary.md:209
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Groups\n"
": Groups are a synonym for departments or processing groups.\n"
"  Incoming tickets can be assigned to groups.\n"
"  Within the group, an owner can be defined, who is then responsible for\n"
"  this ticket. The access to tickets is controlled via the roles. In a role you\n"
"  can define which permission it has based on the different groups.\n"
"  The possible permissions are \"read\", \"create\", \"change\", \"overview\" and\n"
"  \"full\" (or none of them).\n"
msgstr ""
"Grupe\n"
": Grupe su sinonim za odeljenja ili grupe za obradu.\n"
"  Dolazni tiketi se mogu dodeliti grupama.\n"
"  Unutar grupe može se definisati vlasnik, koji tada odgovara za\n"
"  taj tike. Pristup tiketima kontroliše se putem uloga. U ulozi možete\n"
"  definisati koje dozvole ima na osnovu različitih grupa.\n"
"  Moguće dozvole su \"čitanje\", \"kreiranje\", \"izmena\", \"pregled\" i\n"
"  \"puni\" (ili nijedna od njih).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/glossary.md:213
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  If you have worked with the OTRS system in the past, you might remember the\n"
"  principle of \"queues\". The groups in Zammad are the same as the queues in\n"
"  OTRS.\n"
msgstr ""
"  Ako ste ranije radili sa sistemom OTRS, možda se sećate\n"
"  principa \"redova\". Grupe u Zammad-u su iste kao redovi u\n"
"  OTRS-u.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/glossary.md:219
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Icinga\n"
": Icinga is a monitoring system that monitors the availability of an\n"
"  organization's entire system infrastructure.\n"
"  It can be integrated into Zammad so that it triggers a ticket in case\n"
"  of a warning situation.\n"
msgstr ""
"Icinga\n"
": Icinga je sistem za monitorisanje koji prati dostupnost cele\n"
"  sistemske infrastrukture organizacije.\n"
"  Može se integrisati u Zammad tako da pokreće tike u slučaju\n"
"  situacije upozorenja.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/glossary.md:227
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"i-doit\n"
": i-doit is a CMDB (Configuration Management Data Base).\n"
"  It helps you to keep an eye on every piece of the physical and digital\n"
"  infrastructure. A corresponding integration makes it possible to connect\n"
"  it to Zammad, where it adds a new tab to Zammad's ticket sidebar so\n"
"  you can link to existing i-doit objects for easy reference.\n"
"  It also allows you to create Zammad tickets in i-doit.\n"
msgstr ""
"i-doit\n"
": i-doit je CMDB (Configuration Management Data Base).\n"
"  Pomaže vam da održavate pregled nad svakim delom fizičke i digitalne\n"
"  infrastrukture. Odgovarajuća integracija omogućava povezivanje\n"
"  sa Zammad-om, gde dodaje novu karticu u bočnu traku tiketa Zammada tako\n"
"  da možete linkovati postojeće i-doit objekte za lakši pregled.\n"
"  Takođe vam omogućava kreiranje Zammad tiketa unutar i-doit-a.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/glossary.md:231
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Issue-Tracking System\n"
": Issue trackers are usually systems that track processes on a technical level.\n"
"  Two of the best-known examples are GitHub and GitLab.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sistem za praćenje problema\n"
": Sistemii za praćenje problema su obično sistemi koji prate procese na tehničkom nivou.\n"
"  Dva najpoznatija primera su GitHub i GitLab.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/glossary.md:235
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  Zammad is also often referred to as an issue-tracking system.\n"
"  However, as a helpdesk, it focuses on communication at the customer\n"
"  level rather than the technical level.\n"
msgstr ""
"  Zammad se takođe često naziva sistemom za praćenje problema.\n"
"  Međutim, kao helpdesk, fokusira se na komunikaciju na nivou kupca,\n"
"  a ne na tehničkom nivou.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/glossary.md:240
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Kibana <Badge type=\"info\" text=\"on-premise only\" />\n"
": Kibana is a browser-based open-source reporting tool that focuses on data\n"
"  evaluation. It was developed by Elastic, which is why it is not a surprise\n"
"  that it uses data from Elasticsearch for its analytics.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kibana <Badge type=\"info\" text=\"on-premise only\" />\n"
": Kibana je alat za izveštavanje otvorenog koda zasnovan na browseru koji se fokusira na evaluaciju podataka.\n"
"  Razvio ga je Elastic, zbog čega nije iznenađujuće\n"
"  što koristi podatke iz Elasticsearch-a za svoju analitiku.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/glossary.md:243
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  Kibana can be integrated with Zammad, allowing for helpdesk data to be\n"
"  mapped in the reporting tool.\n"
msgstr "  Kibana se može integrisati sa Zammad-om, omogućavajući mapiranje podataka helpdeska u alatu za izveštavanje.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/glossary.md:248
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Knowledge Base\n"
": Think of a very extensive set of FAQs - that's exactly what the\n"
"  Zammad knowledge base is. It collects all important information:\n"
"  definitions, processes, how-tos, organizational charts, etc.\n"
msgstr ""
"Baza znanja\n"
": Zamislite veoma obiman skup FAQ-ova - to je tačno ono što je\n"
"  baza znanja Zammada. Sakuplja svu važnu informaciju:\n"
"  definicije, procese, uputstva, organizacione šeme itd.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/glossary.md:253
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  Knowledge base articles can be either internal or external, so you can\n"
"  either show them to the world (good for information on your product or\n"
"  service, for example) or keep them for your team (e.g. for internal processes\n"
"  or team info).\n"
msgstr ""
"  Članci baze znanja mogu biti ili interni ili eksterni, tako da ih možete\n"
"  prikazati svetu (dobro za informacije o vašem proizvodu ili\n"
"  usluzi, na primer) ili zadržati za vaš tim (npr. za interne procese\n"
"  ili informacije o timu).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/glossary.md:258
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"LDAP\n"
": A Lightweight Directory Access Protocol (LDAP) helps provide information\n"
"  about your users within Zammad. Authentication of users against the LDAP\n"
"  and LDAP role mapping to Zammad roles are also possible.\n"
msgstr ""
"LDAP\n"
": Protokol za pristup imeniku ukratko (LDAP) pomaže u obezbeđivanju informacija\n"
"  o vašim korisnicima unutar Zammada. Autentifikacija korisnika prema LDAP-u\n"
"  i mapiranje LDAP uloga na Zammad uloge su takođe moguće.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/glossary.md:264
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Macro\n"
": A macro is a series of actions. By starting the macro, the actions are\n"
"  triggered and executed, so users don't have to work through each\n"
"  individual step separately. It saves an enormous amount of time and ensures\n"
"  that no step is forgotten.\n"
msgstr ""
"Makro\n"
": Makro je niz akcija. Pokretanjem makra pokreću se i izvršavaju akcije, pa korisnici ne moraju ručno da prolaze kroz svaki\n"
"  pojedinačni korak. Štedi ogromnu količinu vremena i osigurava\n"
"  da se nijedan korak ne zaboravi.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/glossary.md:267
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  You can define your own macros and perform actions based on all available\n"
"  attributes in the ticket.\n"
msgstr ""
"  Možete definisati sopstvene makre i izvršavati akcije na osnovu svih dostupnih\n"
"  atributa u tiketu.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/glossary.md:272
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Main Content\n"
": The middle section of the Zammad layout. Depending on the view you have\n"
"  selected, it shows the dashboard, overviews, the ticket detail view, the\n"
"  create-ticket form or other screens.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/glossary.md:277
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Main Content Footer\n"
": The action row at the bottom of the Main Content area. It holds the primary\n"
"  actions of the currently active view, such as `Create`, `Apply Template` or\n"
"  `Discard Changes` on the create-ticket form.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/glossary.md:282
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Mentions\n"
": Mentions are a Zammad feature that allows you to tag another agent in a\n"
"  ticket. Just type [[@]][[@]] and the name. The selected person will be notified\n"
"  and will be watching the ticket from now on.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pominjanja\n"
": Pominjanja su funkcionalnost Zammada koja vam omogućava da označite drugog agenta u tiketu.\n"
"  Samo ukucajte [[@]][[@]] i ime. Izabrana osoba će biti obaveštena\n"
"  i pratiće tike od sada pa nadalje.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/glossary.md:288
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Migrator / Migration Wizard\n"
": If a company wants to switch from another helpdesk software to Zammad,\n"
"  they often have one concern: What about their existing data?\n"
"  That's why we have built our migration wizards that help with migrating all\n"
"  data.\n"
msgstr ""
"Migrator / Čarobnjak za migraciju\n"
": Ako kompanija želi da pređe sa drugog helpdesk softvera na Zammad,\n"
"  često ima jednu brigu: Šta ćemo sa njihovim postojećim podacima?\n"
"  Zato smo izgradili naše čarobnjake za migraciju koji pomažu pri migraciji svih\n"
"  podataka.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/glossary.md:293
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Monit\n"
": Monit is an open-source monitoring tool that relies on a simple setup and\n"
"  a strong community. You can integrate it with Zammad - this way,\n"
"  a ticket is created every time you receive an email in Monit.\n"
msgstr ""
"Monit\n"
": Monit je alat za monitorisanje otvorenog koda koji se oslanja na jednostavno podešavanje i\n"
"  jaku zajednicu. Možete ga integrisati sa Zammad-om - na ovaj način,\n"
"  tike se kreira svaki put kada primite email u Monit-u.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/glossary.md:296
msgid ""
"Navigation Tab : One element of the primary navigation like **Overviews** or "
"**Knowledge Base**."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/glossary.md:301
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Nagios\n"
": Nagios is another monitoring tool that alerts IT teams when an incident\n"
"  happens. It can be integrated with Zammad so that a ticket is created in\n"
"  case of an alert.\n"
msgstr ""
"Nagios\n"
": Nagios je još jedan alat za monitorisanje koji obaveštava IT timove kada se desi incident.\n"
"  Može se integrisati sa Zammad-om tako da se tike kreira u\n"
"  slučaju alarmiranja.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/glossary.md:306
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"On-Premise\n"
": This term means that Zammad is not provided as a cloud service of the\n"
"  company Zammad, but runs on a server which is controlled by a user or\n"
"  customer of Zammad. Self hosting means the same.\n"
msgstr ""
"On-Premise\n"
": Ovaj termin znači da Zammad nije dostupan kao cloud servis kompanije\n"
"  Zammad, već se pokreće na serveru koji kontroliše korisnik ili\n"
"  kupac Zammada. Samostalno hostovanje znači isto.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/glossary.md:312
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Organization\n"
": An organization is a grouping of customers that operate within the same\n"
"  company or company group.\n"
"  A customer, whose organization is \"sharing\", has access to all tickets of its\n"
"  organization.\n"
msgstr ""
"Organizacija\n"
": Organizacija je grupisanje kupaca koji posluju u okviru iste\n"
"  kompanije ili grupe kompanija.\n"
"  Kupac čija je organizacija \"deljenje\" ima pristup svim tiketima svoje\n"
"  organizacije.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/glossary.md:318
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Owner\n"
": The owner of a ticket is the person responsible for and working on it.\n"
"  The owner can be changed to another agent.\n"
"  In this case, it is recommended to leave a handover note in the ticket so\n"
"  that the new owner knows what to do.\n"
msgstr ""
"Vlasnik\n"
": Vlasnik tiketa je osoba odgovorna za njega i koja na njemu radi.\n"
"  Vlasnika se može promeniti u drugog agenta.\n"
"  U ovom slučaju, preporučuje se ostaviti belešku o predaji u tiketu tako\n"
"  da novi vlasnik zna šta treba da uradi.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/glossary.md:324
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Parent/Child Relationship\n"
": If one ticket results in other subtasks (or additional correspondences),\n"
"  you can split it into several tickets. The main one will then be the parent\n"
"  ticket and the tickets with related subtopics are children.\n"
"  By the way: in the same way, you can also merge two tickets into one.\n"
msgstr ""
"Odnos roditelj/dete\n"
": Ako jedan tike rezultira drugim podzadacima (ili dodatnim korespondencijama),\n"
"  možete ga podeliti na nekoliko tiketa. Glavni će tada biti roditeljski\n"
"  tike, a tiketi sa povezanim podtemama su deca.\n"
"  Usput: na isti način, možete i spojiti dva tiketa u jedan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/glossary.md:330
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Placetel\n"
": Placetel is a Cloud Telephone System that allows users to make phone calls\n"
"  via VoIP. Use your regular phone number and call someone directly on their\n"
"  mobile or landline while still having all communication in one place\n"
"  in Zammad.\n"
msgstr ""
"Placetel\n"
": Placetel je cloudsistema za telefonske pozive koja korisnicima omogućava da obavljaju telefonske pozive\n"
"  preko VoIP-a. Koristite svoj redovni broj telefona i zovite nekoga direktno na njihov\n"
"  mobilni ili fiksni, dok i dalje imate svu komunikaciju na jednom mestu\n"
"  u Zammad-u.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/glossary.md:335
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  Integrating a Placetel account with Zammad provides users with a call log,\n"
"  making the history of their correspondences even more accurate.\n"
"  Callers are identified directly by their caller ID - a key function that\n"
"  saves agents a lot of time when assigning callers.\n"
msgstr ""
"  Integracija Placetel naloga sa Zammad-om daje korisnicima evidenciju poziva,\n"
"  čineći istoriju njihove korespondencije još preciznijom.\n"
"  Pozivaoci se identifikuju direktno preko identifikatora broja pozivaoca - ključna funkcija koja\n"
"  štedi agentima mnogo vremena pri dodeljivanju pozivaoca.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/glossary.md:340
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Primary Navigation\n"
": The primary navigation is the left sidebar in Zammad which contains the\n"
"  taskbar, the search, notifications, knowledge base and eventually more,\n"
"  depending on your system.\n"
msgstr ""
"Navigaciona traka\n"
": Navigaciona traka je leva bočna traka u Zammad-u koja sadrži kartice navigacije,\n"
"  pretragu, obaveštenja i mnogo više stavki, u zavisnosti od vašeg sistema.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/glossary.md:345
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Priority\n"
": Every ticket gets assigned a priority. By default, the priority is 2 (normal).\n"
"  Additionally there are the priorities 1 (low) and 3 (high). You can even\n"
"  add more priorities to your Zammad.\n"
msgstr ""
"Prioritet\n"
": Svaki tike dobija dodeljen prioritet. Podrazumevano, prioritet je 2 (normalan).\n"
"  Pored toga postoje prioriteti 1 (nizak) i 3 (visok). Možete čak\n"
"  dodati više prioriteta u vaš Zammad.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/glossary.md:353
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Release\n"
": Every few months, we release a new version of Zammad which is called a\n"
"  release. Every release adds new features to our software. There are major and\n"
"  minor releases:\n"
"  major releases (such as Zammad 1.0, 2.0, etc.) bring major changes.\n"
"  Minor releases (such as 1.1, 2.1, etc.) are released in the meantime and bring\n"
"  smaller updates.\n"
msgstr ""
"Izdanje\n"
": Svaka nekoliko meseci objavljujemo novu verziju Zammada koja se naziva\n"
"  izdanje. Svako izdanje dodaje nove funkcionalnosti našem softveru. Postoje glavna i\n"
"  sporedna izdanja:\n"
"  glavna izdanja (kao što su Zammad 1.0, 2.0, itd.) donose velike promene.\n"
"  Sporedna izdanja (kao što su 1.1, 2.1, itd.) se objavljuju u međuvremenu i donose\n"
"  manja ažuriranja.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/glossary.md:357
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  In our [release notes](https://zammad.com/en/releases){target=_blank} you can\n"
"  find what features are included in new versions and also important information\n"
"  about what to consider before updating Zammad.\n"
msgstr ""
"  U našim [beleškama o izdanju](https://zammad.com/en/releases){target=_blank} možete\n"
"  pronaći koje su funkcionalnosti uključene u novim verzijama, kao i važne informacije\n"
"  o tome šta treba uzeti u obzir pre ažuriranja Zammada.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/glossary.md:361
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Role\n"
": Every user has an assigned role. By default there are three roles:\n"
"  admin, agent, and customer.\n"
msgstr ""
"Uloga\n"
": Svaki korisnik ima dodeljenu ulogu. Podrazumevano postoje tri uloge:\n"
"  admin, agent i kupac.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/glossary.md:368
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  _Admins_ have the most rights: they can define roles, permissions,\n"
"  and settings for the entire team and instance.\n"
"  _Agents_ can view and edit tickets, but not change any settings other than\n"
"  those of their own profiles.\n"
"  _Customers_ can view their ticket's processing status in their\n"
"  customer interface.\n"
msgstr ""
"  _Administratori_ imaju najveća prava: mogu definisati uloge, dozvole,\n"
"  i podešavanja za ceo tim i instancu.\n"
"  _Agenti_ mogu da pregledaju i uređuju karte, ali ne mogu menjati nikakva podešavanja osim\n"
"  onih u svojim sopstvenim profilima.\n"
"  _Kupci_ mogu da prate status obrade svojih karata u svom\n"
"  korisničkom interfejsu.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/glossary.md:370
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "  You can even add new roles to your Zammad.\n"
msgstr "  Možete čak dodati i nove uloge na svoj Zammad.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/glossary.md:374
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Secondary Navigation\n"
": Refers to an additional menu next to the navigation (e.g. when opening profile\n"
"  settings).\n"
msgstr ""
"Navigacija drugog nivoa\n"
": Odnosi se na dodatni meni pored navigacije (npr. pri otvaranju podešavanja\n"
"  profila).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/glossary.md:378
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Flyout\n"
": The panel that slides in from the right side of the screen for actions such\n"
"  as linking or merging tickets and bulk actions.\n"
msgstr ""
"Bočna traka (Panel)\n"
": Ovo je panel koji se prikazuje sa desne strane za radnje kao što su povezivanje\n"
"  karata ili spajanje karata.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/glossary.md:383
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Sidebar Tab\n"
": In the content sidebar, there are different tabs like \"Customer\",\n"
"  \"Organization\" and \"Ticket\", depending on your system and ticket. These are\n"
"  called sidebar tabs.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kartica bočne trake\n"
": U sadržajnoj bočnoj traci postoje različite kartice kao što su \"Kupac\",\n"
"  \"Organizacija\" i \"Karta\", u zavisnosti od vašeg sistema i karte. One se\n"
"  nazivaju karticama bočne trake.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/glossary.md:385
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "  An active sidebar tab is the currently opened sidebar tab.\n"
msgstr "  Aktivna kartica bočne trake je trenutno otvorena kartica bočne trake.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/glossary.md:391
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Sipgate\n"
": Sipgate is a SaaS solution for internet telephony.\n"
"  The Zammad integration for Sipgate provides users with a detailed call\n"
"  overview. If you have a customer that wants to get connected to a certain\n"
"  agent, the caller log will tell you if this colleague is currently available.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sipgate\n"
": Sipgate je SaaS rešenje za internet telefoniju.\n"
"  Zammad integracija za Sipgate korisnicima pruža detaljan pregled poziva.\n"
"  Ako imate kupca koji želi da se poveže sa određenim\n"
"  agentom, evidencija poziva će vam pokazati da li je ovaj kolega trenutno dostupan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/glossary.md:398
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"SLA\n"
": A Service Level Agreement (SLA) is a contract between an end-user and a\n"
"  company that defines the minimum expected service requirements including\n"
"  quality, availability, and punctuality.\n"
"  They are used to set expectations and hold companies accountable for keeping\n"
"  their promises.\n"
msgstr ""
"SLA\n"
": Sporazum o nivou usluga (SLA) je ugovor između krajnjeg korisnika i\n"
"  kompanije koji definiše minimalne očekivane zahteve za uslugu uključujući\n"
"  kvalitet, dostupnost i tačnost.\n"
"  Koriste se za postavljanje očekivanja i određivanje odgovornosti kompanija za ispunjavanje\n"
"  njihovih obećanja.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/glossary.md:402
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  You can easily set up SLAs in Zammad and define parameters such as the time\n"
"  for the first response, an update, and a solution. Once the deadline has been\n"
"  reached, the ticket will escalate.\n"
msgstr ""
"  SLA možete lako podesiti u Zammadu i definisati parametre kao što je vreme\n"
"  za prvi odgovor, ažuriranje i rešenje. Čim istekne rok, karta će biti eskalirana.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/glossary.md:408
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"S/MIME\n"
": S/MIME is the most widely-supported method for secure email communication.\n"
"  By activating and configuring this integration in Zammad, outgoing messages\n"
"  can be signed and encrypted and incoming messages can be decrypted and their\n"
"  signature checked.\n"
msgstr ""
"S/MIME\n"
": S/MIME je najviše podržavani metod za bezbednu elektronsku komunikaciju.\n"
"  Aktiviranjem i konfigurisanjem ove integracije u Zammadu, izlazne poruke\n"
"  mogu biti potpisane i šifrovane, a dolazne poruke dešifrovane i provera njihovih\n"
"  potpisa.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/glossary.md:413
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"SSO\n"
": Single-sign-on (SSO) allows you to access all your systems and devices with\n"
"  just one login. There are various providers that make this process easy and\n"
"  secure. Zammad currently supports SSO via different providers.\n"
msgstr ""
"SSO\n"
": Jedinstveno prijavljivanje (SSO) omogućava vam pristup svim vašim sistemima i uređajima uz\n"
"  samo jedno ulogovanje. Postoji mnogo različitih pružalaca usluga koji olakšavaju ovaj proces i\n"
"  čine ga bezbednim. Zammad trenutno podržava SSO putem različitih pružalaca.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/glossary.md:420
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"State\n"
": Every ticket has a state which reflects the current progress of resolving the\n"
"  issue. The state of a ticket can be changed manually or automatically based\n"
"  on automation or SLA. Each state has a state type. There are four state types\n"
"  by default and they are color-coded. You can even add additional states to\n"
"  your Zammad.\n"
msgstr ""
"Status\n"
": Svaka karta ima status koji odražava trenutni napredak u rešavanju\n"
"  problema. Status karte se može menjati ručno ili automatski na osnovu\n"
"  automatizacije ili SLA. Svaki status ima svoj tip statusa. Postoje četiri tipa statusa\n"
"  podrazumevano i oni su označeni bojama. Možete čak dodati i dodatne statusе na\n"
"  svoj Zammad.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/glossary.md:424
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Taskbar\n"
": The section of the primary navigation which contains the taskbar tabs for\n"
"  your opened tickets, users, organizations and the detailed search.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/glossary.md:428
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Taskbar Tab\n"
": A single tab in the taskbar. Clicking the tab brings the corresponding\n"
"  ticket, user, organization or search into the main content area.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/glossary.md:436
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Tags\n"
": Tags help you to categorize tickets. You can define them based on your use\n"
"  case. For example, if you're a retail business, your tags could be based on\n"
"  your product categories to help you organize tickets by the type of product\n"
"  they refer to.\n"
"  But they could also be based on the type of request, e.g. refund, delivery\n"
"  issue, complaint.\n"
msgstr ""
"Oznake\n"
": Oznake vam pomažu da kategorizujete karte. Možete ih definisati na osnovu vaše\n"
"  upotrebe. Na primer, ako ste trgovinska kompanija, vaše oznake mogu biti bazirane na\n"
"  kategorijama proizvoda kako biste organizovali karte po tipu proizvoda\n"
"  na koji se odnose.\n"
"  Ali mogu biti bazirane i na tipu zahteva, npr. povrat novca, problem sa\n"
"  isporukom, pritužba.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/glossary.md:439
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  Tags can be queried in conditions in an automation and assigned\n"
"  automatically, for example depending on keywords in the ticket title.\n"
msgstr ""
"  Oznake se mogu upitivati u uslovima automatizacije i dodeljivati\n"
"  automatski, na primer na osnovu ključnih reči u naslovu karte.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/glossary.md:447
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Text Module\n"
": If you find that you send the same answers over and over again,\n"
"  you can save yourself a lot of work and create a text module.\n"
"  This way, you just need to type the [[:]][[:]] shortcut in an article and all\n"
"  available text modules are shown from which you can select the desired one.\n"
"  You can limit the search results by adding parts of the text module's name,\n"
"  keywords or content after the [[:]][[:]].\n"
msgstr ""
"Tekstualni modul\n"
": Ako uočite da šaljete iste odgovore iznova i iznova,\n"
"  možete sebi uštedeti mnogo posla tako što ćete kreirati tekstualni modul.\n"
"  Na ovaj način, potrebno je samo da ukucate prečicu [[:]][[:]] u članak i svi\n"
"  dostupni tekstualni moduli će se prikazati iz kojih možete izabrati željeni.\n"
"  Možete ograničiti rezultate pretrage dodavanjem delova naziva tekstualnog modula,\n"
"  ključnih reči ili sadržaja nakon [[:]][[:]].\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/glossary.md:450
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  For example, here at Zammad, we have a text module with the shortcut\n"
"  `::ilff`, which turns into `I look forward to your feedback`.\n"
msgstr ""
"  Na primer, ovde u Zammadu imamo tekstualni modul sa prečicom\n"
"  `::ilff`, koji se pretvara u `Veselim se vašem odzivu`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/glossary.md:455
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(Ticket) Template\n"
": If you create many similar tickets, you can create a template for them. This\n"
"  is helpful for introductions to your product/service or for drawing up an\n"
"  offer.\n"
msgstr ""
"Šablon (karte)\n"
": Ako kreirate mnogo sličnih karata, možete za njih napraviti šablon. Ovo\n"
"  je korisno za predstavke vašeg proizvoda/usluge ili za sastavljanje\n"
"  ponude.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/glossary.md:461
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"User\n"
": A user is any user of the ticket system. Each user has assigned\n"
"  permissions, which allow them to access certain areas and information.\n"
"  Users can have various roles, with the standard options being agent, admin,\n"
"  and customer.\n"
msgstr ""
"Korisnik\n"
": Korisnik je bilo koji korisnik sistema za karte. Svaki korisnik ima dodeljene\n"
"  dozvole koje mu omogućavaju pristup određenim oblastima i informacijama.\n"
"  Korisnici mogu imati različite uloge, pri čemu su standardne opcije agent, administrator,\n"
"  i kupac.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/glossary.md:467
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Webhooks\n"
": Webhooks are an easy way for systems to communicate with each\n"
"  other and allow you to send data to any other application.\n"
"  They allow you to inform a third party system about new information in Zammad\n"
"  (e.g. sending a notification for new and updated tickets to your Mattermost).\n"
msgstr ""
"Webhook-ovi\n"
": Webhook-ovi su jednostavan način za komunikaciju sistema međusobno\n"
"  i omogućavaju vam slanje podataka bilo kojoj drugoj aplikaciji.\n"
"  Omogućavaju da obvestite sistem treće strane o novim informacijama u Zammadu\n"
"  (npr. slanje notifikacije za nove i ažurirane karte na vaš Mattermost).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/glossary.md:470
#, fuzzy
msgid "Zammad : Zammad is the greatest helpdesk in the world. Period."
msgstr "Zammad : Zammad je najbolji helpdesk na svetu. Tačka."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/glossary.md:471
#, no-wrap
msgid "</VPGlossary>\n"
msgstr "</VPGlossary>\n"

#. type: Title #
#: src/en/reference/graphql.md:1 src/en/reference/graphql.md:6
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "GraphQL API"
msgstr "GraphQL API"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/graphql.md:12
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"In addition to Zammad's [REST API](rest-api/intro), you can fetch, "
"manipulate and create data via the powerful and open-source [GraphQL API]"
"(https://graphql.org/){target=_blank} too."
msgstr ""
"Pored [REST API-ja](rest-api/intro) u Zammadu, možete preuzimati, menjati i "
"kreirati podatke putem moćnog i otvorenog izvornog [GraphQL API-ja](https://"
"graphql.org/)."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/graphql.md:16
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"This documentation isn't intended to cover everything about GraphQL. It "
"should give you a basic understanding about how you can fetch and create/"
"manipulate data to build upon. For a comprehensive guide, have a look at "
"[GraphQL's documentation](https://graphql.org/learn/){target=_blank}."
msgstr ""
"Ova dokumentacija ne pokriva sve o GraphQL-u. Treba da vam pruži osnovno "
"razumevanje kako možete preuzimati i kreirati/menjati podatke za dalje "
"izgradnje. Za iscrpne uputstva, pogledajte [dokumentaciju GraphQL-a](https://"
"graphql.org/learn/)."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/graphql.md:20
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"GraphQL is used by many web services, even big ones. It became some kind of "
"industry standard because of its efficiency and features. You can precisely "
"request the data you require which minimizes unnecessary data transfers and "
"searching the needle in a haystack."
msgstr ""
"GraphQL koriste mnoge veb servise, uključujući i velike. Postao je vrsta "
"industrijskog standarda zbog svoje efikasnosti i funkcija. Možete precizno "
"zatražiti podatke koji su vam potrebni, čime se minimiziraju nepotrebni "
"prenosi podataka i štedi vreme."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/graphql.md:23
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Fetching the Zammad GraphQL schema (called introspection) enables "
"autocomplete and client-side validation while writing requests."
msgstr ""
"Preuzimanje GraphQL šeme Zammada (nazvano introspekcija) omogućava "
"automatsko dopunjavanje i validaciju na klijentskoj strani dok pišete "
"zahteve."

