#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:11
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "Conceptual Overview"
msgstr "Преглед функција"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:16
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Like every other web application out there, Zammad has its own logic for "
"signing users up, storing their passwords, authenticating them, and managing "
"their sessions."
msgstr ""
"Kao i svaka druga veb aplikacija, Zammad ima sopstvenu logiku za "
"registraciju korisnika, čuvanje lozinki, autentifikaciju i upravljanje "
"sesijama."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:22
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"If your IT department keeps its own user identity store (like Active "
"Directory), Zammad's SSO support allows you to leverage that existing auth "
"system so that anyone with an account on your local intranet will 1) "
"automatically have an account in Zammad and 2) be able to log in with a "
"single click."
msgstr ""
"Ako vaše IT odeljenje održava sopstveno skladište identiteta korisnika "
"(poput Active Directoryja), SSO podrška u Zammadu omogućava iskorišćavanje "
"tog postojećeg sistema autentifikacije, tako da svako ko ima nalog na vašoj "
"lokalnoj intranetu 1) automatski će imati nalog u Zammadu i 2) moći će da se "
"prijavi jednim klikom."

#. type: Fenced div block (tip)
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:23
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If you don't have this IT infrastructure but still want one-click\n"
"login, you can use alternatives like Github, Google, Facebook and more.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ako nemate ovu IT infrastrukturu, ali želite prijavu jednim klikom,\n"
"moguće je koristiti alternative kao što su GitHub, Google, Facebook i druge.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:28
#, no-wrap
msgid "How Does it Work?"
msgstr "Како то уствари функционише?"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:34
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Once enabled, single sign-on activates an endpoint at `https://"
"your.zammad.host/auth/sso`. When the Zammad server receives a GET request at "
"this endpoint with a valid username in **any one of the following** "
"entities, it creates a new session for that user:"
msgstr ""
"Nakon aktiviranja, jedinstvena prijava omogućava endpoint na `https://"
"your.zammad.host/auth/sso`. Kada Zammad server primi GET zahtev na ovom "
"endpointu sa validnim korisničkim imenom u **bilo kom** od sledećih polja, "
"kreira novu sesiju za tog korisnika:"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:38
#, fuzzy
msgid "an `X-Forwarded-User` request header"
msgstr "`X-Forwarded-User` zaglavlje zahteva"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:38
#, fuzzy
msgid "a `REMOTE_USER` web server environment variable"
msgstr "promenljiva okruženja veb servera `REMOTE_USER`"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:38
#, fuzzy
msgid "an `HTTP_REMOTE_USER` web server environment variable"
msgstr "promenljiva okruženja veb servera `HTTP_REMOTE_USER`"

#. type: Fenced div block (info)
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:39
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Wait. SSO allows you to sign in with only a username?**\n"
"\n"
"In principle, yes.\n"
"\n"
"**How is that okay?**\n"
"\n"
"In this guide, we configure our web server (Apache) to intercept all\n"
"requests to the `/auth/sso` endpoint. Instead of forwarding them to\n"
"Zammad, Apache initiates a three-sided login process (_Kerberos\n"
"authentication_) between the itself, the user, and the Active\n"
"Directory server.\n"
"\n"
"If Active Directory doesn't recognize the user or their password,\n"
"Zammad never sees the request, and the session is never created.\n"
"\n"
"**What does this all mean?**\n"
"\n"
"It means there are many ways you could set up SSO—you don't need to\n"
"follow this guide or even use Active Directory or Kerberos—but if you\n"
"don't know what you're doing, you're going to end up with a _massive_\n"
"security hole.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Ček. SSO omogućava prijavu samo korisničkim imenom?**\n"
"\n"
"U principu, da.\n"
"\n"
"**Kako je to u redu?**\n"
"\n"
"U ovom vodiču konfigurisali smo veb server (Apache) da prekine sve\n"
"zahteve ka `/auth/sso` endpointu. Umesto da ih prosledi na\n"
"Zammad, Apache inicira proces prijave sa tri strane (_Kerberos\n"
"autentifikacija_) između sebe, korisnika i servera Active\n"
"Directoryja.\n"
"\n"
"Ako Active Directory ne prepozna korisnika ili njegovu lozinku,\n"
"Zammad nikada ne vidi zahtev i sesija se nikada ne kreira.\n"
"\n"
"**Šta sve ovo znači?**\n"
"\n"
"To znači da postoji mnogo načina kako možete postaviti SSO—ne morate\n"
"pratiti ovaj vodič niti koristiti Active Directory ili Kerberos—ali ako\n"
"ne znate šta radite, na kraju ćete imati _ogroman_\n"
"propust u bezbednosti.\n"

#. type: Fenced div block (tip)
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:65
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Too busy to handle it on your own?**\n"
"\n"
